  "problems": "",
  "rationale": "Setting --aligner star_rsem adds 'star_rsem' to the indices to prepare. Because no --rsem_index is given, RSEM_PREPAREREFERENCE_GENOME builds one, while STAR_GENOMEGENERATE still builds the same STAR index for ALIGN_STAR. STAR_ALIGN switches to the RSEM-specific ext.args, which changes the genome BAM and therefore re-runs all sorting, markduplicates, QC, bigWig, StringTie and MultiQC tasks. Quantification moves from QUANTIFY_BAM_SALMON and DESEQ2_QC_BAM_SALMON to QUANTIFY_RSEM, its tximport/SummarizedExperiment steps and DESEQ2_QC_RSEM, while the FASTQ-based Salmon pseudo-alignment is unchanged."
